# Workers Static Assets serves a matching asset WITHOUT invoking the worker, so
# a cache-control header set in worker.js never reaches these files. `_headers`
# is the mechanism that does apply to them, and it costs no worker invocation.
#
# /geo and /data are rebuilt by atlas/etl and redeployed, never edited in place,
# so they are safe to cache hard. The county topology and the county series are
# the two big fetches on the page; an hour of freshness plus a day of
# stale-while-revalidate is the difference between a warm reload and a cold one.
/geo/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400
/data/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400
/lib/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=600
